            <ArticleTitle>An unusual case of endometrial trocar site implantation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>992-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present the case of a 35-year-old woman with a history of apparent bilateral hernia who had a surgical intervention that included a diagnostic laparoscopy converted to open laparotomy. The patient experienced endometrial implants exclusively at trocar sites. This case is cited as validation of the pneumoperitoneum-induced free cell implantation theory, or the so-called aerosolization theory.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
